# ECS Stack Conventions

Three stack flavours: `ecs-service` (long-running), `ecs-ondemand` (RunTask), `ecs-scheduled` (EventBridge-triggered). They share most patterns.

## Required dependencies

`ecs_cluster`, `vpc`, plus any application data store (`ddb-*`, `s3-*`, `rabbitmq-broker`) the task uses.

## Subnet tier pattern

```hcl
locals {
  app_alias   = "mercury"
  subnet_tier = "private"   # "isolated" | "private" | "public"
}

inputs = {
  subnet_ids = (local.subnet_tier == "isolated" ? dependency.vpc.outputs.isolated_subnet_ids :
                local.subnet_tier == "private"  ? dependency.vpc.outputs.private_subnet_ids  :
                local.subnet_tier == "public"   ? dependency.vpc.outputs.public_subnet_ids   : [])

  vpc_security_group_ids = (local.subnet_tier == "isolated" ? [dependency.vpc.outputs.isolated_security_group_id] :
                            local.subnet_tier == "private"  ? [dependency.vpc.outputs.private_security_group_id]  :
                            local.subnet_tier == "public"   ? [dependency.vpc.outputs.public_security_group_id]   : [])
}
```

Default app workloads to `private`. `public` is only for ALB-fronted resources, `isolated` for databases.

## Required service inputs

`app_alias`, `cluster_arn`, `desired_count` (services only), `task_cpu`, `task_memory`, `network_mode = "awsvpc"`, `container_image`, `container_port`, `cpu_architecture`, `operating_system_family`.

## Container image

Use the ECR URI form `{account}.dkr.ecr.{region}.amazonaws.com/{repo}:{tag}`. Avoid `:latest` outside sandboxes; pin a tag from CI.

## Container secrets

```hcl
container_secrets = [
  { "name" : "ENV_NAME",  "valueFrom" : "/ENV/NYX/ENV_NAME" },
  { "name" : "LOG_LEVEL", "valueFrom" : "/ENV/MERCURY/LOG_LEVEL" },
]
```

`valueFrom` is the SSM path. Add the matching parameter in the corresponding `ssm_param` stack, then declare the dependency here.

## IAM policies

- `task_exec-policy_arns` — managed policies the **execution role** needs (always include `AmazonECSTaskExecutionRolePolicy` and `AmazonSSMReadOnlyAccess`).
- `task_role-policy_arns` — managed policies the **task role** needs.
- `custom-role_policy` — inline JSON for app-specific permissions; scope `Resource` ARNs by `${include.inputs.account_id}` and `${include.inputs.region}`, never `*` for cross-account writes.

## Anti-patterns

- Hardcoded subnet/SG IDs.
- Missing `desired_count` on services (causes drift).
- Empty `container_command` written as `[""]` instead of `[]`.
